# Event-Driven Development

Cross-module communication uses the event bus exclusively. Modules never import from each other directly.

## Event Naming Convention

Format: `{module}.{entity}.{action}` (dot-separated, lowercase)

```typescript
'authentication.user.registered'
'authentication.user.logged.in'
'identity.user.created'
'identity.user.updated'
```

## Publishing Events

### 1. Define Event Schema (`src/common/event-manager/application/schemas/{module}.events.ts`)

```typescript
import { IsUUID, IsEmail } from 'class-validator';
import { EventSchema } from '../../domain/events/event.interface';

class EntityActionPayload {
  @IsUUID()
  entityId: string;
}

export const ModuleEventSchemas = {
  ENTITY_ACTION: {
    eventName: 'module.entity.action',
    schema: new EntityActionPayload(),
    version: '1.0.0',
    module: 'module-name',
    description: 'Emitted when entity action occurs',
  } as EventSchema<EntityActionPayload>,
} as const;
```

### 2. Create Event Class (`{module}/domain/events/{entity}.events.ts`)

```typescript
import { BaseEvent } from 'src/common/event-manager';

export class EntityActionEvent extends BaseEvent<typeof ModuleEventSchemas.ENTITY_ACTION.schema> {
  private readonly eventPayload: typeof ModuleEventSchemas.ENTITY_ACTION.schema;

  constructor(entityId: string, params?: Omit<EventMetadata, 'version' | 'timestamp'>) {
    super(ModuleEventSchemas.ENTITY_ACTION, params);
    this.eventPayload = { entityId };
  }

  toJSON() {
    return this.eventPayload;
  }
}

export { ModuleEventSchemas as MODULE_EVENTS } from 'src/common/event-manager';
```

### 3. Publish from Use Case

```typescript
@Inject(EVENT_BUS_TOKEN)
private readonly eventBus: EventBusPort;

await this.eventBus.publish(new EntityActionEvent(entity.id));
```

## Subscribing to Events

Create handler classes in `{module}/application/handlers/`:

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class EntityActivityHandler {
  constructor(private readonly someUseCase: SomeUseCase) {}

  @OnEvent(MODULE_EVENTS.ENTITY_ACTION.eventName)
  handleEntityAction(event: EntityActionEvent) {
    return this.someUseCase.execute(event);
  }
}
```

## Rules

- Event handlers must be idempotent — processing the same event twice produces the same result
- Event handlers delegate to use cases, never contain business logic directly
- Use `correlationId` in event metadata for tracing across module boundaries
- Event payloads use `class-validator` decorators for runtime validation
- Register all event schemas in `src/common/event-manager/application/schemas/`
- Export event schemas index from `src/common/event-manager/application/schemas/index.ts`
- Re-export schemas as `MODULE_EVENTS` from the domain events index
